n class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.</span> \n"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08re6aud01"}]}, {"type": "template_override", "content": 2}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 10, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn9le02ob08re7pdf01.pdf"}]}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nWatch some trailers about bee movies.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le02ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "text": "Experts are often asked by science forum writers whether the bumblebee is really in danger of becoming extinct. As an entomologist, I have been involved in this field of research for decades. I am afraid that I must say yes, bee populations are under threat. One possible result of this is that the other species can become extinct when a food chain is disrupted by external forces.", "id": 1}, {"time": "30000", "image": "engenn9le02ob08re2img02.jpg", "text": "The process that is leading to the extinction of the bumblebee is not completely clear. It may be due to the loss of their natural habitats and pesticides used by farmers against other insects that destroy their crops. The ideal habitat for the bumblebee is a field of natural wild flowers. However, most farming today involves large fields and farmers  are often sticking to a single crop. If there are not enough plant varieties available, there is not enough nectar for bees to survive. In addition, beekeepers think that some pesticides have caused bees to have trouble finding their way home ...", "id": 2}, {"time": "74000", "image": "engenn9le02ob08re2img03.jpg", "text": "SOS ... bumblebee populations are being decimated by pesticides in some areas. There is somewhat of a problem with finding a solution to bee extinction. Some growers have tried to pollinate the fields themselves using helicopters and other equipment. Sometimes bees are given extra protein by growers to have enough energy to pollinate. However, these solutions are clearly not enough. If more research is not done into  the processes involved in maintaining bee populations, we may have to kiss our sweet honey goodbye. The extinction of many species has been caused by a failure to act.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "11500", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\">When do you use a conditional sentence?</span>", "id": 1}, {"time": "29000", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\">When do you use the zero conditional?</span>", "id": 2}, {"time": "50900", "image": "", "text": "<Span class=\"bullet\">When do you use the first conditional?</span>", "id": 3}, {"time": "73000", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\">When do you use the second conditional?</span>", "id": 4}, {"time": "104000", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\">When do you use the third conditional?</span>", "id": 5}], "video_src": "engenn9le02ob08re3vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Environment"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Extinction of the Bumblebee"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe environmental change in social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "  Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences With <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use conditional sentences to describe the result of something that might happen or might have happened but didn't."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Zero conditional</span> sentences have two<span class=\"strong\"> Present Simple </span> verbs, one in the <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">if</span> clause</span> and one in the <span class=\"strong\">main clause</span>. You use this conditional when the result will always happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the form:<br/> <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">If</span> + Present Simple, ... Present Simple.</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">first conditional</span> sentences to talk about things which might happen in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the form:<br/> <div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"italic\">if</span> + Present Simple, ... <span class=\"italic\">will</span> + infinitive</div> <br> You can use <span class=\"strong\">modals</span> (can, may, might ) other than will in the main clause of a sentence in the first conditional."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> second conditional</span> to talk about \"unreal\" or impossible events.<br/> The <span class=\"strong\">second conditional</span> uses the <span class=\"strong\">Past Simple</span> after if, then 'would' and the infinitive:<br/><br/> <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">if</span> + Past Simple, ... <span class=\"italic\">would</span> + infinitive</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">third conditional</span> to talk about the past. It is used to describe a situation that didn't happen, and to imagine the result of this situation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">if</span> + Past Perfect, ... <span class=\"italic\">would</span> + <span class=\"italic\">have</span> + past participle</div>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If more research is not done into the process of bee extinction, we may have to kiss our sweet honey goodbye."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If an extinct species had been food for another organism, that organism would then have become at risk for extinction. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If people had known of the negative impact of farming in sensitive area, they would have considered other alternatives."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Continuous / Present Perfect "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense </span> to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way.<br/>The <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> is used to talk about actions that are happening in the present moment but will soon finish.</p><p>You can also use these tenses in the passive form.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous tense</span> when you talk about:<ul><li>things which are happening at the moment of speaking</li><li>temporary situations</li><li>temporary or new habits</li><li>to talk about people in pictures and photos</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">are living</span> in a changing world.<br/>This process<span class=\"strong\"> is leading </span> to the extinction of the bumblebee.<br/>Bumblebees <span class=\"strong\">are being decimated</span> by pesticides. </span>(passive) "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about experience.<br/>When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Some growers <span class=\"strong\">have tried</span> to pollinate the fields themselves using helicopters and other equipment.<br/>Bumblebee populations <span class=\"strong\">have been destroyed</span> by human interest.</span> (passive)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The extinction of many species <span class=\"strong\">has been caused</span> by the lack respect of man to the planet species.</span> (passive)"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "entomologist "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a scientist who studies and does research on insects"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As an entomologist, I have been involved in this field of research for decades."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you are writing about bees and their population decline."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "under threat "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "at risk of death or extinction"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Bee populations are under threat."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "habitat "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the natural home of a plant or animal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Due to the loss of their natural habitats, bees are becoming extinct."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pesticide "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a chemical substance used to kill insects and small animals that destroy crops"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Pesticides are being used by farmers to protect their  crops."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nectar "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the sweet liquid that bees collect from flowers"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is not enough nectar for bees to survive."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pollinate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to give a flower or plant pollen so that it can produce seeds"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some growers have tried to pollinate the fields themselves."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "beekeeper "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is in charge of growing bees to make honey products"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Beekeepers think that some pesticides have caused bees to have trouble finding their way home."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "protein "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one of several natural substances that exist in food used to build muscle and hair"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sometimes bees are given extra protein by growers."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "extinction "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when a particular type of animal or plant stops existing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The extinction of many species has been caused by a failure to act."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le02ob08aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Watch 4 trailers about different bee movies."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What kinds of issues do they bring up in the movies? Write a summary of what you saw."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss the issue of declining bee populations with your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I watch and reflect on 4 trailers about bees."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a summary of the trailers."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the issue of declining bee populations with my partner."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le02ob08re1img01.jpg"}]}